ding","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#destructive","content":"Destructive"},"338":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-12","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#semantic-tokens","content":"Semantic Tokens"},"339":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-13","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#surfaces","content":"Surfaces"},"340":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-14","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Actions"},"341":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-15","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Status"},"342":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-16","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Form"},"343":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-17","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Charts"},"344":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-18","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Sidebar"},"345":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-19","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#vittal-extensions","content":"Vittal Extensions"},"346":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-20","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#avatar-palette","content":"Avatar Palette"},"347":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-21","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#tag-palette","content":"Tag Palette"},"348":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-22","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Vittal Design follows the shadcn/ui\nnaming convention for its semantic layer. Colors are defined under\ntokens/ (Style Dictionary), built into src-v2/styles/tokens/generated.css\nas CSS custom properties on :root, with dark overrides on .dark,\nand exposed to Tailwind via @theme inline (--color-*)."},"349":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-23","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Primitive scales (--primary-50…900, --grayscale-100…900,\n--grayscale-opacity-100…900, --success-100…900, etc.) — internal\nfoundation. Reach for these when you need a specific shade for\ncharts, illustrations, or fine-grained tinting. Tailwind utility:\nbg-primary-500, text-grayscale-700, etc."},"350":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-24","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Semantic tokens (--background, --primary, --card,\n--destructive, …) — the public API. These describe intent\nand pair with -foreground siblings for legible content on the\nsurface. Tailwind utility: bg-primary text-primary-foreground."},"351":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-25","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#overview","content":"Component tokens (--avatar-*-fg, --tag-*-solid) — closed\npalettes used by specific components."},"352":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-26","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#dark-mode","content":"Add class=\"dark\" to an ancestor, usually <html>. With\nnext-themes, set\nattribute=\"class\". The theme does not follow\nprefers-color-scheme. Reinstall @vital-design/vital-theme so\ncssVars.dark is written into the app stylesheet."},"353":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-27","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#dark-mode","content":"Every color swatch on this page shows two values: L is the light\nvalue and D is the dark value. Each chip is drawn on its own\nmode's page color, so translucent values look the way they render."},"354":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-28","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#what-changes-under-dark","content":"Primitive scales take their dark values from\ntokens/dark/colors.json. A scale class such as\ntext-grayscale-opacity-800 or bg-primary-500 switches on its own."},"355":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-29","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#what-changes-under-dark","content":"Semantic tokens that alias a scale are rebuilt from the dark\nscale: primary → primary.500, foreground →\ngrayscale-opacity.900, border → grayscale-opacity.200."},"356":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-30","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#what-changes-under-dark","content":"A few semantic tokens set their own dark value in\ntokens/dark/colors.json: background, card, and popover\n(#232327), and input (#444447)."},"357":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-31","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#what-changes-under-dark","content":"These keep their light value: literal *-foreground whites,\nthe avatar and tag palettes below, and the shadow and\ngradient tokens on Effects."},"358":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-32","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#what-changes-under-dark","content":"The .dark ancestor paints background and foreground, so text\nthat sits on the page uses the dark ink. It also sets\ncolor-scheme: dark, so native controls, scrollbars, and browser focus\noutlines render dark."},"359":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-33","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"Paper uses bg-background, not bg-white."},"360":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-34","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"When a fill turns light in dark mode, such as bg-grayscale-700 or\nbg-grayscale-opacity-700, put text-background on it so the text\nturns dark with it. Tag, Tooltip, and solid Toast do this."},"361":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-35","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"Child elements that fade the parent's text color use\ntext-current/90, not text-white/90."},"362":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-36","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"bg-white and text-white stay white. Use them for marks that must\nstay white, such as switch, slider, and radio thumbs, and for text on\nsaturated fills that keep one value in both modes."},"363":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-37","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"When a step lacks contrast in one mode, pick another step with the\ndark: variant. The data table selection bar uses\ntext-info-400 dark:text-info-200."},"364":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-38","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#writing-components-for-both-modes","content":"Don't hardcode colors with arbitrary values such as\nbg-[#f8f8f9]. Use the nearest scale step."},"365":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-39","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#primary","content":"The primary palette is a blue scale used for interactive elements,\nbuttons, focus states, and key affordances."},"366":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-40","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale","content":"The default grayscale palette is fully solid — use it whenever the\nsurface must be opaque (popovers, tooltips, toasts, solid chips)."},"367":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-41","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#grayscale-opacity","content":"The opacity variant uses rgba(35, 35, 50, α) so it tonally adapts\nover any background. Use it for hover tints, dividers, disabled fields,\nand other states where translucency is desired. --grayscale-opacity-900\nis the only solid hex."},"368":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-42","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#success","content":"Positive feedback, confirmations, \"saved\" states."},"369":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-43","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#info","content":"Informational messaging and neutral status indicators."},"370":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-44","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#warning","content":"Caution states — soft warnings that don't block flow."},"371":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-45","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#destructive","content":"Errors, destructive actions, hard validation failures."},"372":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-46","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#semantic-tokens","content":"Intent-based aliases that point to primitive colors. Each surface\nships with a paired -foreground token — use them together so text\nremains legible regardless of theme overrides."},"373":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-47","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#surfaces","content":"Page chrome, cards, popovers, and muted/accent regions. background\nis the page; card and popover are elevated containers; muted\nand accent are subtle background tints (e.g. table stripes, hover\nstates)."},"374":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-48","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#actions","content":"Brand action surfaces. primary is the dominant call-to-action;\nsecondary is the alternative button surface."},"375":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-49","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#status","content":"Feedback colors paired with foreground for legible content."},"376":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-50","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#form","content":"Borders, input strokes, and focus rings. border is the 0.08 hairline\nfor dividers and single edges, and it is also the default color of a bare\nborder class. border-overlap is solid, for edges that stack or cross,\nsuch as avatar outlines in a group or tree rails, where a translucent line\nwould darken. input strokes form fields; ring paints focus outlines."},"377":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-51","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#charts","content":"Five-step palette for data visualization. Defaults rotate through\nprimary → success → warning → info → destructive so chart series\ninherit brand color regardless of theme overrides."},"378":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-52","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Application sidebar shell slots (shadcn-compatible). Used by the\nSidebar primitive utilities such as\nbg-sidebar, text-sidebar-foreground, and border-sidebar-border.\nProduct blocks may override individual slots (for example\n[--sidebar:transparent] on the cloud shell)."},"379":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-53","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Slot"},"380":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-54","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"Default alias"},"381":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-55","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar"},"382":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-56","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"grayscale.100"},"383":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-57","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-foreground"},"384":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-58","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"grayscale.900"},"385":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-59","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-primary"},"386":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-60","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"primary.500"},"387":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-61","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-primary-foreground"},"388":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-62","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"white"},"389":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-63","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-accent"},"390":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-64","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"primary.50"},"391":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-65","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-accent-foreground"},"392":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-66","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"primary.700"},"393":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-67","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-border"},"394":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-68","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"grayscale-opacity.200"},"395":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-69","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"--sidebar-ring"},"396":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-70","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#sidebar","content":"primary.300"},"397":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-71","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#vittal-extensions","content":"Tokens unique to Vittal Design with no shadcn equivalent. Kept\nunprefixed for ecosystem consistency (matching how Origin UI ships\nits extensions)."},"398":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-72","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#avatar-palette","content":"Each named avatar color exposes three tokens — fg (text /\ninitials), border, and bg. Used by AvatarRoot color=\"…\".\nThese tokens have light values only, so avatars keep the same colors\nunder .dark."},"399":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors-73","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/colors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/colors#tag-palette","content":"Each named tag color exposes solid (text / icon) and tint\n(background). Used by Tag color=\"…\". These tokens have light\nvalues only, so tags keep the same colors under .dark."},"400":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","type":"page","content":"Effects","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Design Tokens"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects"},"401":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-0","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","content":"Elevation shadows, focus rings, button shadows, and gradient tokens."},"402":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-1","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#elevation","content":"Elevation"},"403":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-2","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#focus-rings","content":"Focus Rings"},"404":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-3","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#button-shadows","content":"Button Shadows"},"405":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-4","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#gradients","content":"Gradients"},"406":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-5","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","content":"These tokens have light values only. They don't change under .dark,\nso shadows are hard to see on dark surfaces. See\nColors → Dark mode."},"407":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-6","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#elevation","content":"Four elevation shadows for layering content. accent is the\nsoftest; top-level is reserved for modal-class surfaces."},"408":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-7","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#focus-rings","content":"Outer rings rendered as box-shadow so they don't shift layout.\nMatch the colour to the control's intent:"},"409":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-8","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#focus-rings","content":"--shadow-focus-* — solid 2px ring tinted with the matching 200\nstep"},"410":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-9","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#focus-rings","content":"--shadow-focus-ring-* — softer translucent ring used for\ninline-edited controls (inputs, search bars)"},"411":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-10","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#button-shadows","content":"Pre-baked drop shadows that match the five button themes. The\n-active variants are the pressed-state counterparts."},"412":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-11","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#gradients","content":"A single gradient family used for primary buttons and accent\nsurfaces."},"413":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects-12","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/effects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/effects#gradients","content":"--gradient-primary-button is an alias of --gradient-primary\nprovided for forward compatibility — both currently resolve to the\nsame linear-gradient(45deg, #33CFFF 0%, #0E86FE 100%)."},"414":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","type":"page","content":"Border Radius","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Design Tokens"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius"},"415":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-0","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","content":"Corner radius tokens shared by inputs, buttons, cards, and dialogs."},"416":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-1","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#tokens","content":"Tokens"},"417":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-2","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#usage-guidance","content":"Usage Guidance"},"418":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-3","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#combining-with-sizes","content":"Combining With Sizes"},"419":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-4","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#tokens","content":"Vittal Design exposes six radius steps via CSS custom properties.\nThey are mapped to Tailwind's rounded-* utilities, so you can use\neither form."},"420":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-5","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#usage-guidance","content":"Token"},"421":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-6","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#usage-guidance","content":"Recommended usage"},"422":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-7","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#usage-guidance","content":"--radius-none"},"423":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-8","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/design-tokens/radius#usage-guidance","content":"Square corners — utility surfaces, inline edge-to-edge groups"},"424":{"id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius-9","page_id":"/docs/design-tokens/radius","t