agination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#client-side-pagination","content":"For in-place updates, use render to compose a native button and keep the current page in your own state. Buttons retain their native Enter and Space behaviour. The preview at the top uses this pattern; its Code tab shows the full example."},"2334":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-19","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#client-side-pagination","content":"Pagination does not calculate page ranges, load data, or own a current-page state. Keep the page count, visible page numbers, and data updates together in the consuming screen."},"2335":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-20","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#more-pages","content":"Use PaginationEllipsis for gaps in the visible range. Pass the hidden page numbers and onPageSelect. It renders the same button as the other page controls and opens a menu of those pages. This example keeps the current group of five pages visible. Choosing a page inside that group does not move the group. When ellipses appear on both sides, the first and last page numbers stay in those menus; the icon buttons still jump to those pages. Three-digit page numbers expand to fit."},"2336":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-21","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#more-pages","content":"The preview's Code tab includes its page-range calculation. The calculation stays outside the Pagination primitive."},"2337":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-22","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#first-last-and-disabled-controls","content":"PaginationFirst and PaginationLast follow the same API as PaginationPrevious and PaginationNext. Place each in a PaginationItem."},"2338":{"id":"/docs/components/paginat