t dialog and render is ignored."},"3024":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-48","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#keyboard","content":"⌘B / Ctrl+B toggles the sidebar (desktop open state or mobile sheet)."},"3025":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-49","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#cookie--open-state","content":"SidebarProvider writes a sidebar_state cookie when open state changes (for optional cross-page sync). It does not read the cookie on mount — initial state comes from defaultOpen or a controlled open prop. This keeps SSR and first paint predictable; read the cookie yourself only if your app needs restore-on-load."},"3026":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-50","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#cookie--open-state","content":"Set cookieName to write under another name, or cookieName={null} to write no cookie. To persist state some other way, use onOpenChange."},"3027":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-51","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#theme-css-variables","content":"Sidebar colors use shadcn-compatible semantic slots. Defaults are defined in tokens/semantic/color.json and emitted to src-v2/styles/tokens/generated.css (imported via globals.css). See Colors → Sidebar."},"3028":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-52","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#theme-css-variables","content":"Variable"},"3029":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-53","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#theme-css-variables","content":"Default"},"3030":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar-54","page_id":"/docs/components/sidebar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/sidebar#theme-css-variables","content":"--sidebar"},"3031":{"id":"/docs/components/sidebar